WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:05.000
Fixed-time guarantees can fail under repeated monitoring.
One checked event can cover repeated looks.

00:05.000 --> 00:09.500
The library then builds outward through VC generalization, PAC-Bayes,
e-processes, and dependent-data inference.

00:09.500 --> 00:14.000
One proof stack moves from fixed samples through adaptive selection,
repeated looks, and dependent paths.

00:14.000 --> 00:18.500
VC growth bounds and metric entropy
feed complexity estimates.

00:18.500 --> 00:23.000
Two checked routes: a VC tail bound
and a metric-entropy integral bound.

00:23.000 --> 00:27.500
PAC-Bayes prices posterior selection
with relative entropy.

00:27.500 --> 00:32.000
One event covers every allowed posterior and declared tilt;
the declared bound fails with probability at most delta.

00:32.000 --> 00:36.500
Confidence sequences and e-processes
remain valid under repeated looks.

00:36.500 --> 00:41.000
One event covers every time and every declared choice;
an e-process exceeds 1/alpha with probability at most alpha.

00:41.000 --> 00:45.500
Choose from the observed prefix.
Fix the next score before the next state.

00:45.500 --> 00:50.000
With a supplied invariant law and Poisson potential,
the correction connects path evidence to stationary risk.

00:50.000 --> 00:54.500
One controlled-queue case study: 4,608 coordinates
reduce to one exact hit-rate parameter.

00:54.500 --> 00:59.000
For every physical row, total variation equals the hit-rate gap
inside the declared family; this is not a membership test.

00:59.000 --> 01:03.000
Four representative theorem anchors: VC ERM, metric entropy,
anytime PAC-Bayes, and adaptive trajectories.

01:03.000 --> 01:06.000
Declarations and files are pinned at 501fee4;
the queue is one application of the library.

01:06.000 --> 01:12.000
FormalSLT: reusable Lean infrastructure for statistical guarantees,
from classical generalization to adaptive data.
